COPY public.sections (id, meeting_id, "position", kind, title, about, summary, start_seconds, end_seconds, is_vote, relevant, signals) FROM stdin;
ebd7e42b-c1d9-4494-834f-655615959e71	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	0	introduction	Pledge of Allegiance and Call to Order	This section covers the opening of the meeting with the Pledge of Allegiance and initial attendance acknowledgments.	Participants began the meeting by reciting the Pledge of Allegiance together. Following the pledge, members indicated their presence by responding to the roll call. This completed the introductory procedures to formally open the session.	0.56	32.56	f	t	["data_center", "siting"]
592ff998-9b17-44be-8567-b04f01d2ddbc	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	1	agenda	Council Announcements and Public Hearings	This section covers council announcements and scheduled public hearings for the meeting.	The floor was opened for any announcements from council members, but none were brought forward. Additionally, it was noted that no public hearings were scheduled for the evening.	35.2	43.44	f	t	["data_center", "siting"]
6482f517-9bb2-4529-9b68-1aeac573175d	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	2	agenda	Meeting Communications and Pre-Agenda Presentations	This section covers communications included in the packet and provides a summary of presentations delivered during the pre-agenda meeting.	The packet communications included a letter withdrawing a planning commission application and a certificate of completion for an arena project. Presentations included an overview of the online budget booklet prior to an upcoming public hearing. An update was also given regarding business park infrastructure improvements and a grant application for road changes.	43.68	124.24	f	t	["data_center", "siting"]
db048ce3-7356-4bbc-8e09-17fa36caee08	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	3	agenda	Public Comment on Proposed Data Center	This section features public comments expressing strong opposition to a proposed data center and concerns regarding local property taxes.	Members of the public voiced significant opposition to a proposed data center, citing widespread community disapproval, non-disclosure agreements, and high estimated energy usage. Speakers also highlighted potential impacts on nearby residential and agricultural land, including health risks, noise, and a lack of communication with neighbors. Additionally, concern was raised about a steep increase in local property taxes.	124.4	481.76	f	t	["data_center", "jobs", "noise", "siting", "tax"]
ed0f730e-96dc-4612-9b92-f84ccdd87756	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	4	agenda	Concerns Over Industrial Development Zoning	This section features public testimony expressing opposition to a proposed large-scale commercial industrial development project and associated zoning changes.	A speaker criticized large corporations for using non-disclosure agreements and pressuring local officials to bypass thorough environmental reviews for development projects. Concerns were raised that a proposed 234-acre industrial site in Hermantown is unsuitable due to its location in a wooded residential area with sensitive trout streams and floodplains. The city was urged to pause and re-evaluate the project's impact on the local community.	483.04	617.6	f	t	["data_center", "jobs", "noise", "siting", "tax"]
0d7d7855-77a1-44d8-a861-f82efe7f54dc	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	5	agenda	Public Comment on Council Conduct and Data Center Proposal	This section features a public comment criticizing city leadership regarding a data center approval and announcing a candidacy for city council.	A resident expressed frustration with city leaders, alleging disrespect toward citizens and calling into question the approval of a data center despite community opposition. The speaker highlighted concerns about rising utility costs, corporate influence, and potential safety risks associated with the project. Additionally, the resident proposed options for replacing current council members and announced an intention to run for city council in 2026.	618.56	866.56	f	t	["data_center"]
456ef33c-732b-4eb8-ad19-755766c6ca81	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	6	agenda	Public Comment on Data Center Concerns	A resident expressed concerns regarding the transparency of a proposed data center and its potential political impact on local leaders.	The speaker highlighted community frustration over the perceived lack of transparency surrounding the data center project, noting that residents feel their home is under attack. While acknowledging the leadership's public service intentions, the speaker warned that continuing with the current approach could harm their political standing. The statement concluded with a call to avoid personal attacks while carefully reconsidering the ongoing strategy.	866.88	993.44	f	t	["data_center", "noise"]
889f93f1-daf1-408b-b1c4-b2e5dea6d0f9	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	7	agenda	Concerns Regarding Proposed Data Center Noise and Emissions	A speaker thanked the city council members for their service before expressing concerns about the noise and environmental impacts of proposed data centers.	The discussion focused on the potential negative effects of low-frequency sound from data centers, which can travel up to two and a half miles and disturb nearby residents. Concerns were also raised regarding the loud noise levels and air pollution produced by backup diesel and jet-powered generators. The speaker urged the city to consider these health and noise issues carefully when negotiating with the company.	994.08	1190.96	f	t	["data_center", "jobs", "noise"]
3d298432-96c4-40cc-aae1-c39c32bf1d9f	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	8	agenda	Public Comment on Proposed Data Center	This section features public feedback regarding a proposed data center development.	A resident voiced opposition to the project, arguing that local community members clearly do not support it. They asserted that proponents primarily seek tax cuts or financial gain and often do not reside in the area. Finally, local leadership was urged to listen to the desires of the public.	1192.32	1233.52	f	t	["data_center", "jobs"]
eed006b9-c56a-4c25-888b-25f6c0024fed	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	9	agenda	Public Comment on Proposed Data Center	A community member delivers a public comment opposing the location and handling of a proposed data center project.	The statement urges developers to relocate heavy industrial data centers to former mining lands on the Iron Range to protect residential neighborhoods, natural resources, and the local tourism economy. Concerns were expressed regarding a lack of government transparency, the use of non-disclosure agreements, and insufficient public review time for affected residents. The comment concludes with a call for honest dialogue and a sustainable development vision that aligns with community values.	1233.68	1655.44	f	t	["data_center", "jobs", "noise"]
99742332-f5e2-4cab-be39-e515a59729f2	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	10	agenda	Public Comment Opposing Proposed Hyper Data Center	A community member speaks out against a proposed hyper data center project and details its potential impacts on the surrounding neighborhood.	The speaker discussed the emotional, personal, and environmental strain that the proposed hyper data center is causing local residents. They highlighted concerns about losing the natural peace and beauty of the area to industrial development. Finally, they urged local officials to engage in constructive dialogue with the community and halt the project.	1655.92	1942	f	t	["data_center", "noise"]
9e7730e0-0a01-4a77-92e5-43f22303fca3	2e6ef3ee-a942-4b2f-897c-0fc3311f1924	0	introduction	Meeting Call to Order and Roll Call	This section covers the opening of the public meeting, including the Pledge of Allegiance and roll call.	The meeting was officially called to order by the presiding officer. Attendees stood to recite the Pledge of Allegiance to the flag. Following the pledge, roll call was conducted to record attendance.	1.199	33.51	f	f	[]
e2d38e77-426c-4a41-8c09-1c0bc7498c30	2e6ef3ee-a942-4b2f-897c-0fc3311f1924	1	agenda	here. Announcements. Do any counselors	\N	\N	33.52	41.35	f	f	[]
668de69f-5204-4072-ace9-9f4f2cc57b87	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	11	agenda	Public Comments on Proposed Data Center	This section features public comments from community members regarding a proposed data center project.	Residents voiced concerns about the environmental, financial, and health impacts of the proposed data center, including noise pollution and potential secrecy by local officials. A proposal was made to utilize the facility's waste heat to provide free or low-cost heating to nearby homes if the project moves forward. Speakers urged the council to reject the project permits and prioritize the interests of local constituents.	1942.16	2497.04	f	t	["data_center", "power"]
36966356-4759-442d-8632-b8ee9e718325	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	12	agenda	Public Comments on Proposed Data Center Project	This section consists of public comments from local residents expressing strong opposition to a proposed data center in the community.	Community members voiced concerns about environmental risks, including wetland loss, heavy water and power consumption, and potential well contamination. Speakers also criticized the city's handling of the project, alleging a lack of transparency, improper zoning changes, and an insufficient environmental review process. Several individuals requested a more thorough environmental impact study and urged officials to reject the project.	2499.28	3802.88	f	t	["data_center", "jobs", "noise", "siting", "water"]
99855c6e-30af-49ce-a8cd-5ecd3514f9a1	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	13	agenda	Closure of Public Discussion	This section marks the conclusion of the public comment segment of the meeting.	The public discussion portion of the meeting was officially brought to a close. Participants were informed that no further public comments would be taken at this point. The meeting then prepared to move forward with the next agenda items.	3805.68	3808.72	f	t	["data_center"]
ad551092-2795-4ae5-8f21-70684a05e0e6	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	14	agenda	Recess Announcement for Chamber Exit	This section details a brief ten-minute recess announced to allow attendees to leave the chamber before official business continues.	The meeting paused for a ten-minute break prior to addressing upcoming motions and ordinances. Audience members who wished to leave were given time to exit the room without disrupting the proceedings. Those interested in the remaining agenda items were invited to stay for the continuation of the meeting.	3809.04	3829.2	f	t	["data_center"]
9782bd46-0a05-45cf-a93b-e644f21d1b6c	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	15	agenda	Consent Agenda Approval	This section covers the review and vote on the city council consent agenda.	The consent agenda included the approval of previous city council continuation minutes and general city warrants totaling $844,293 for the first half of November 2025. A motion to approve the agenda was introduced and seconded. A roll call vote was then conducted to record the votes on the motion.	3829.92	3875.12	t	t	["data_center"]
1803f782-7a6a-42fe-8d8d-cd9a7535111f	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	16	agenda	Consideration of City Ordinances	This section covers the second reading of an ordinance regarding accepted city streets and the first reading of a cable television franchise renewal.	The council addressed an update to the city code to incorporate newly constructed roads into the official list of accepted streets. A first reading was also presented to renew a ten-year cable television franchise agreement, which includes a franchise fee on subscriptions. Public input was solicited for both proposed ordinances during the meeting.	3875.84	4045.36	t	t	["data_center"]
a36d9190-08b6-4d74-8c39-be34b1e9cece	cfcca4db-3923-4d63-9f00-32aaafedc520	17	agenda	Public Input on Mediacom Ordinance	This section covers a call for public input regarding a cable television ordinance for Mediacom Minnesota LLC.	The presiding officer opened a public comment period regarding Ordinance 2025-20, which concerns a cable television franchise with Mediacom Minnesota LLC. Attendees were offered multiple opportunities to provide input during the first reading of the ordinance. No public comments were submitted during this portion of the meeting.	4045.68	4080.32	f	t	["data_center", "power"]
